.TH PATSCC 1 "2026-10-24" "ATS/Postiats 0.4.3" "ATS2 Manual"
.SH NAME
patscc \- compile ATS2 programs to executables
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B patscc
.RI [ options "] " "file.dats ..."
.br
.B patscc \-o
.I prog prog.dats
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B patscc
is the driver of the ATS2 compiler. For each ATS file it runs
.BR patsopt (1)
to produce a C file, and then it runs the C compiler on the C files. The
options that it does not know are passed to the C compiler, so
.B patscc \-O2 \-o prog prog.dats
works as expected.
.PP
It needs no flag for a program that uses the prelude: the C compiler is
.B ${CC:\-cc}
with
.B \-std=c99 \-D_GNU_SOURCE
and the include and library paths of
.BR PATSHOME ;
libc
.BR malloc (3)
is the allocator. (The usage text printed by
.B patscc \-\-help
still calls the programs
.I atscc
and
.IR atsopt :
they are
.B patscc
and
.BR patsopt .)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the usage of
.BR patscc .
.TP
.B \-hats
Print the usage of
.BR patsopt .
.TP
.B \-vats
Print the version of
.BR patsopt .
.TP
.B \-ccats
Only compile the ATS files into C files; do not run the C compiler on them.
.TP
.B \-tcats
Only typecheck the ATS files.
.TP
.B \-\-gline
Passed to
.B patsopt
to generate line pragmas in the generated C code.
.TP
.B \-verbose
Print each command line that is executed.
.TP
.B \-cleanaft
Remove each C file that
.B patsopt
generated once the C compilation is finished.
.TP
.BI \-atsccomp " command"
Use the next argument as the C compilation command (instead of the value
of
.BR PATSCCOMP ).
.TP
.BI \-DATS " name" [ =value ]
Pass the definition to
.B patsopt
only.
.TP
.BI \-DDATS " name" [ =value ]
Pass the definition to both
.B patsopt
and the C compiler.
.TP
.BI \-IATS " dir"
Pass the include path to
.B patsopt
only.
.TP
.BI \-IIATS " dir"
Pass the include path to both
.B patsopt
and the C compiler.
.TP
.BI \-fsats " file"
Treat the file as static ATS code (a file with the suffix
.I .sats
needs no flag).
.TP
.BI \-fdats " file"
Treat the file as dynamic ATS code (a file with the suffix
.I .dats
needs no flag).
.TP
.B \-\-tlcalopt\-disable
Passed to
.B patsopt
to disable tail-call optimization.
.TP
.B \-\-constraint\-ignore
Passed to
.B patsopt
to ignore constraint solving (dangerous).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PATSHOME
The root of the ATS2 installation. The scripts that
.B make install
puts in
.I PREFIX/bin
set it.
.TP
.B CC
The C compiler (default
.BR cc ).
.TP
.B PATSCCOMP
The whole C compilation command; it replaces the default one.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $PATSHOME/ccomp/runtime
The C headers that the generated code includes.
.TP
.I $PATSHOME/ccomp/atslib/lib/libatslib.a
The runtime library.
.SH NO GARBAGE COLLECTOR
There is no garbage collector. Heap data must be linear
.RB ( datavtype ,
.BR list_vt ,
.BR option_vt ,
.BR arrayptr ,
.BR cloptr ,
.BR stream_vt ),
and the compiler rejects a
.B datatype
with a non-nullary constructor, a
.B cloref
closure, a boxed tuple or record,
.B $delay
and
.BR $list_t .
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
patscc \-o hello hello.dats
patscc \-O2 \-g \-fsanitize=address \-o prog prog.dats
CC=clang patscc \-o prog prog.dats
patscc \-ccats prog.dats     # only makes prog_dats.c
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR patsopt (1),
.BR myatscc (1)
.PP
The documentation of the repository: README.md, INSTALL, doc/GUIDE/.
